<title>SINGAPORE: India sells Apr Vizag naphtha to Vitol at -$25/T.</title>
<headline>India sells Apr Vizag naphtha to Vitol at -$25/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has sold by tender 25,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) to Dutch trader Vitol at $25.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, free-on-board (fob) Vizag on the east coast, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender for the cargo lifting mid-April closed on April 3 and was valid until April 4.</p>
<p>IOC's last LAN cargo from Vizag, lifting March 30-April 1 was awarded to European major Shell at $17.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, fob.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
